solution.text:
From Einstein's photoelectric equation,
$$
\begin{array}{l}
h v=W+e V \\
W=\text { Work function }
\end{array}
$$
$v=$ Frequency of incident photon 
$V=$ Stopping potential 
For a photon of frequency $v_{1},$
$$
h v_{1}=W+e V_{1}
$$
For photon of frequency $v_{2}$
$$
h v_{2}=W+e V_{2}
$$
Divided Eq. (i) by Eq. (ii),
$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{h v_{1}}{h v_{2}} &=\frac{W+e V_{1}}{W+e V_{2}} \\
\frac{v_{1}}{v_{2}} &=\frac{W+e V_{1}}{W+e V_{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$
$\Rightarrow W v_{1}+e V_{2} v_{1}=W v_{2}+e V_{1} v_{2}$
Solving above equation, $\Rightarrow \quad e=\frac{W\left(v_{2}-v_{1}\right)}{V_{2} v_{1}-V_{1} v_{2}}$
